From 563c15942a39a5f56d994451174a4ab80dbf425b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 08:35:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 45/58] topk: follow-up fixes to the persistent top-k kernels

- Counter enum declared above the decode template (two-phase lookup).
- Emission-fault flag set atomically.
- Close the legacy large tie loop with a block barrier (inherited).
- Large-path fault injectors registered as hashed passthroughs.
- The tensor-free counter-slots op registered for CompositeExplicitAutograd.
- Tie measurements recorded only on rows neither fault verdict failed.
- Tests scoped to the properties the build promises.
